    "output": "This Solution Blueprint defines the Phase 1 scope for Archlin\u2019s investment in integrated supply management capabilities for its specialty chemicals manufacturing business.\n\nArchlin currently operates with an integrated planning environment with some automation, supported by SAP S/4HANA as the enterprise ERP system, but continues to experience poor inventory planning as a key business pain point.\n\nThe Phase 1 implementation is focused on Supply Management and is intended to strengthen Archlin\u2019s ability to determine total requirements for products and raw materials, generate supply plans, and support procurement execution through purchase order and purchase requisition planning processes.\n\nThe solution direction for Archlin is to use Kinaxis Maestro capabilities to support supply planning and order management processes, including planning through bill of material structures where applicable, identifying supply requirements for purchased products and raw materials, and improving planning visibility across supply management activities.\n\nArchlin\u2019s supply management solution will be designed to work with SAP S/4HANA as the system of record for relevant enterprise data, with planning inputs, master data, transactional data, and planning outputs aligned to the implementation design confirmed during blueprinting.\n\nThe blueprint establishes the functional foundation for Archlin\u2019s Phase 1 implementation by documenting the intended planning process, key assumptions, integration considerations, and expected business outcomes for supply management.\n\nThe implementation will prioritize standard Kinaxis Maestro capabilities where fit for Archlin\u2019s supply management requirements, with any extensions or configuration decisions evaluated against Archlin\u2019s business rules, SAP S/4HANA integration needs, and the objective of improving inventory planning performance.\n\nArchlin\u2019s expected outcomes from Phase 1 include improved visibility to supply requirements, better alignment between demand signals and supply actions, more structured planning of purchased materials, and a stronger foundation for inventory planning governance within the specialty chemicals manufacturing supply chain.\n\nDetails such as Archlin\u2019s specific site list, product hierarchy, supplier segmentation, bill of material scope, planning calendars, and detailed integration objects are and will need to be confirmed during the implementation phase.",
