  "1.2": {
    "status": "generated",
    "output": "Current State of Business\n\nArchlin operates in the specialty chemicals manufacturing industry with SAP S/4HANA as its core ERP system and a planning environment that is currently partially automated, siloed, and heavily dependent on Excel-based processes.\n\nArchlin\u2019s current planning process requires planners to spend significant time consolidating forecasts and planning inputs from multiple regions, and Archlin does not currently have a centralized planning platform across North America and Europe.\n\nArchlin\u2019s current forecast accuracy is approximately 68%, and limited forecast visibility contributes to inventory levels that are higher than target.\n\nArchlin\u2019s manual and spreadsheet-based planning processes create delays in monthly planning cycles and limit timely collaboration between sales, operations, and supply chain teams.\n\nArchlin\u2019s key business pain point for this phase is poor inventory planning, including limited visibility to inventory targets, excess and obsolete exposure, slow-moving inventory, stock-out recovery, and root-cause analysis of inventory exceptions.\n\nArchlin is investing in Kinaxis RapidResponse to establish a more integrated planning capability aligned with its SAP S/4HANA environment, with Phase 1 focused on Supply Management.\n\nArchlin\u2019s Phase 1 Supply Management scope is expected to improve planner visibility into demand and supply alignment, supply orders, material shortages, constraints, inventory positions, and exceptions that require action.\n\nArchlin\u2019s target solution direction includes the ability for planners to view period-ending inventory in value and volume, define and adjust inventory targets, identify slow-moving, excess, and obsolete inventory, analyze stock-out recovery, simulate corrective actions, and collaborate on inventory exceptions.\n\nArchlin\u2019s implementation will require master data and integration alignment with SAP S/4HANA so that supply planning, inventory planning, planning parameters, bills of material, part-source data, constraints, and supply orders can support effective decision-making in Kinaxis RapidResponse.\n\nArchlin\u2019s expected business outcomes from the Phase 1 Supply Management implementation include improved inventory planning discipline, better cross-functional visibility, faster exception identification, stronger support for supply decision-making, and a more scalable foundation for future planning maturity.",
