    "output": "1.3 Scope\n\nArchlin's Phase 1 scope for the RapidResponse implementation is focused on Supply Management for its specialty chemicals manufacturing business.\n\nArchlin's current planning environment is partially automated and operates across siloed systems, with poor inventory planning identified as the primary business pain point to be addressed in this phase.\n\nArchlin's blueprint scope defines the prescribed supply management processes, planning capabilities, and supporting resources required to establish the baseline for the future-state planning model.\n\nArchlin's RapidResponse solution scope includes establishing a common planning terminology and operating model for Archlin business and IT stakeholders, aligned to foundational RapidResponse planning capabilities and prescribed data interfaces.\n\nArchlin's source system for the scoped planning integration is SAP S/4HANA, and the detailed integration design, data mapping, and automation approach will be defined as part of the solution and technical blueprint activities.\n\nArchlin's implementation scope includes documenting the user stories, analytics, and solution configuration details required to support the Supply Management release.\n\nArchlin's solution blueprint will be updated during implementation to reflect approved requirement changes and solution design decisions for the scoped release.\n\nArchlin's blueprint at technical go-live is intended to represent both the confirmed requirements and the implemented RapidResponse solution design for the Phase 1 Supply Management scope.\n\nArchlin's expected outcome from this scope is an improved foundation for inventory planning, better visibility into supply management processes, and a more integrated planning environment than the current siloed planning landscape.\n\nArchlin's specific site, plant, product-family, geography, and detailed organizational scope is &lt;information not available in Archlin source documents&gt;.\n\nArchlin's Phase 1 scope does not include test results within this blueprint section.",
